  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The power gain is defined as the ratio of change in output power and the change in input power.<br />Since, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>VI</mi></math>.</p><p><br />Therefore, Power gain = Current gain X Voltage gain<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><br />Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>k&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>k&#937;</mi></math>.<br />Hence, Power gain <math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
